<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Haere Ra Waltz Song (Maewa Kaihau)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1935</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Search Me, O God (J. Edwin Orr)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody (the hymn tune &quot;Māori&quot;)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Now Is the Hour (Gracie Fields)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1948</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recorded; world-wide hit</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Now Is the Hour (Bing Crosby)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1947</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recorded; No. 1 in 1948</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">My Thanks to You (Connie Francis)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1959</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recorded on</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Now Is the Hour (Deane Waretini album)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recorded on, title</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Now Is the Hour (Māori Television series about Deane Waretini)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">title</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The New Look soundtrack (The 1975)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Project Hail Mary (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2026</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in (Turakina Māori Girls' College Choir recording)</span></li></ul></section>
